@attribute [Route(GlobalValues.Path_Overview_Introduction)]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Page_Title_Overview_Introduction</PageTitle>

<h1 class="page-heading">@GlobalValues.Page_Heading_Overview_Introduction</h1>

<p>
    Blazor Ramp is an open-source project that aims to provide a set of free, accessibility-first Blazor components, each delivered individually via NuGet. 
    While each component is self-contained, they all utilise the Blazor Ramp Core package. This core dependency provides a centralised Live Region service that ensures 
    stable, consistent announcements via the ARIA Live API. Additionally, the Core package includes an Announcement History component, which maintains a 
    rolling log of the last twenty live region announcements for user review.
</p>
<p>
    Each component or NuGet package is designed to be both agnostic and self-contained, with no dependencies on third-party scripts or CSS libraries. To continue 
    this theme of self-reliance, this documentation site also avoids third-party scripts or CSS libraries; it is a Blazor WASM standalone project hosted on 
    GitHub Pages.
</p>

<p>
    This site provides all the documentation for Blazor Ramp, from installation and usage to theming the components. It will be continuously updated as the project 
    progresses — so please check back regularly.
</p>
<p>
    Currently, this project is developed solely by myself, Paul Kent (aka code-dispenser).
</p>
<p>
    If there is anything you would like to see in the future, or features you feel are missing from released components, please submit a request via the 
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" target="_blank" href="@GlobalValues.Web_Site_Path_GitHub_Repo">Blazor Ramp GitHub repository (opens in new window)</a> issues. 
    Alternatively, make a post on Reddit and I will generally chime in.
</p>

<p>
    Please spread the word about the project; the more developers who start using the components, the more accessible Blazor sites will hopefully become - a step in the 
    right direction.
</p> 
<p>
    I am going to leave the <a target="_blank" class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" href="@GlobalValues.Web_Site_Path_Component_Test">Blazor Ramp Component Test (opens in new window)</a> site running for future components and, time permitting, will restructure it to house both past and present components.
    This will allow developers and end users alike to see if the components work for their particular device setup at anytime.
</p>
<p>
    Thanks for stopping by.
    <br />
    <br />
    <i>Paul Kent</i>
</p>
<p>
    <b>Thank you</b> to TestingBot for providing an open-source plan so I can access a variety of real devices when testing. Please pay them a visit to see the services they offer.
</p>
<p>
